[quote="phantaskippy"]

I have made my own environment decks, but the problem with that is if you have a bunch of decks involved it becomes pretty easy to guess what that top card is.

[/quote]

Say for the point of entertaining the idea you have sleeves with black backs.&nbsp;

I have also played with the idea of mixing hero decks.&nbsp; For a one player game, you could put three character cards in front of you, then mix those three decks.&nbsp; Draw whatever number of cards seems fair (and wouldn&#39;t be too overwhelming for the player as far as options) to create a hand.&nbsp; The reason I say this is that having 12 cards in my hand would paralyze me with options...&nbsp; Villian and environment decks are the same as regular play.&nbsp; Then play whatever 3 cards you like, use whatever 3 powers you like, draw 3 cards.&nbsp;

The above setup would favor one-shots, or tend to build one character at the expense of others depending on how you&#39;d like to strategize.&nbsp; Search cards would become super valuable.&nbsp; You think that would work or do you think it would be far too easy?

[quote="phantaskippy"]

I&#39;ve wanted to make a Dinosaur invasion environment deck, some contrived scenario where Ambuscade somehow lets loose tons of Dinosaurs in Megalopolis where you could mix those decks together and play two each environment turn.That could be really fun.&nbsp;

[/quote]

I do really like that idea!&nbsp;

Yeah, I guess mashing all the hero decks together does destroy the framework of turns where you&#39;d have to find an arbitrary time for seeing when the &quot;start of turn,&quot; &quot;play phase,&quot; and &quot;power phase&quot; effects and actions happen to each character card.&nbsp; Would make things more difficult than mashing them together simplifies.

It makes me think about how The Sentinels team might work, actually.&nbsp; Like how does that deck deal with the fact that there are four targets upon which equipment need to be placed?&nbsp; Could you build up one member with equipment to the detriment of others?&nbsp; Are you ever really hurting to find the one-shot that corresponds to the character card that is built up with said equipment? I know this is no mystery to the playtesters though.&nbsp; Maybe all the one shots and equipment are placed on the team generally, but i&#39;d consider that a squandered opportunity to add complexity. :D

&nbsp;
